// Two meshing spur gears for a reduction: a pinion of `teeth` teeth and a
// wheel of round(ratio x teeth), placed at the center distance
// m·(z1 + z2)/2 and turned so that a tooth of each sits in the other's
// gap. It echoes the teeth, the actual ratio (the wheel's teeth over the
// pinion's, which rounding may move off the one asked for) and the center
// distance. A design uses it with
//
//     use <mechanical/gear_pair.c2f>
//     gear_pair(ratio = 3, mod = 1, thickness = 6);
//
// `mod` is the module (the language keeps the word `module` for itself).
// With `center` true, the point halfway between the axes is at the
// origin, the pinion on -x and the wheel on +x; else the pinion's axis is
// at the origin and the wheel's on +x. The gears are those of
// `spur_gear.c2f`, each tooth thinned by `backlash` (0.15 mm by default,
// for FDM printing) so that they turn freely at the exact distance.

// @description Helper to model a gear reduction: gear_pair(ratio, mod,
// @description teeth, thickness) places a pinion and a wheel of involute spur
// @description gears at the right center distance, m·(z1 + z2)/2, meshing,
// @description and echoes the actual ratio.
// @spec center distance: module x (pinion teeth + wheel teeth) / 2
// @spec ratio: the wheel's teeth over the pinion's, rounded to whole teeth
// @spec pressure angle: 20°
// @spec backlash: 0.15 mm per tooth by default, for FDM printing
// @source https://www.iso.org/standard/22643.html ISO 53, the basic rack tooth profile
// @source https://khkgears.net/new/gear_knowledge/gear_technical_reference/calculation_gear_dimensions.html KHK, the calculation of gear dimensions (center distance)

use <spur_gear.c2f>

/* [Gears] */
// The reduction: the wheel turns this many times slower than the pinion.
ratio = 3; // [1:0.1:10]
// The module, in millimeters.
mod = 1; // [0.5:0.25:5]
// The pinion's teeth.
teeth = 17; // [8:1:60]
// The gears' thickness.
thickness = 5; // [1:0.5:50]

// The wheel's teeth for `ratio` with a pinion of `teeth` teeth.
function gear_pair_teeth(ratio, teeth) = round(ratio * teeth);

// The distance between the axes of two gears of module `mod`, `z1` and
// `z2` teeth.
function gear_center_distance(mod, z1, z2) = mod * (z1 + z2) / 2;

// A pinion of `teeth` teeth and a wheel `ratio` times bigger, of module
// `mod`, `thickness` thick, meshing: see the file's opening comment.
module gear_pair(ratio = 3, mod = 1, teeth = 17, thickness = 5, center = true, bore = 0,
                 wheel_bore = 0, pressure_angle = 20, backlash = 0.15) {
    assert(ratio >= 1, "gear_pair: the ratio is 1 or more: the wheel is the bigger gear");
    z1 = teeth;
    z2 = gear_pair_teeth(ratio, teeth);
    a = gear_center_distance(mod, z1, z2);
    echo(str("gear_pair: ", z1, " and ", z2, " teeth, ratio ", z2 / z1, ", center distance ", a, " mm"));
    translate([center ? -a / 2 : 0, 0, 0]) {
        spur_gear(mod, z1, thickness, bore, pressure_angle, backlash);
        // The wheel's gap faces the pinion's tooth on +x.
        translate([a, 0, 0]) rotate(180 + 180 / z2)
            spur_gear(mod, z2, thickness, wheel_bore, pressure_angle, backlash);
    }
}

gear_pair(ratio, mod, teeth, thickness);
